 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 533549,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Are these triangles similar? Find the lengths of sides <span data-math=\"x\">x</span> and <span data-math=\"y\">y</span> to prove your answer.\n<figure>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/16b3b8154fdd1650.png\" alt=\"Two right triangles. In the first triangle, the legs measure y and 18 meters. The hypotenuse measures 30 meters. In the second triangle, the legs measure 8 meters and x. The hypotenuse measures 10 meters. The top angles in both triangles are congruent.\">\n</figure>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Step 1: You know the corresponding angles have equal measures from the drawings. That is enough to determine similarity.</p>\n<p>Step 2: Set up proportions to find the missing values.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"\\frac{{10}}{{30}} = \\frac{x}{{18}}\"></span></td>\n<td>Multiply.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"30x = 180\"></span></td>\n<td>Divide.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"x = 6{\\rm{\\ m}}\"></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"\\frac{y}{8} = \\frac{{30}}{{10}}\"></span></td>\n<td>Multiply.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"10y = 240\"></span></td>\n<td>Divide.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"y = 24{\\rm{\\ m}}\"></span></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"x = 6\">x = 6</span>, <span data-math=\"y = 24\">y = 24</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
